    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 293,
        "text": "Welcome back, everyone. Today we are testing the limits of a broad conclusion. Last week our seminar group looked at a simple claim: \"Students who take notes by hand remember more than students who type.\" That claim came from one small study, and today we ask: how far does it really go?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "f013f57c1e98a2feda4263266248882081b17b0da9fdda861f322091927547d7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 303,
        "sourceEnd": 421,
        "text": "Can I start with a question? When you say \"remember more,\" do you mean immediately after the lecture, or a week later?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "864a1a212dae600265b976c22c4f2781c734bf6ae9122a50736377cc35566052",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 429,
        "sourceEnd": 583,
        "text": "Good question. The original study tested recall after one week. So the conclusion is about one-week recall, not about all memory. That is our first limit.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "22a2f084cd34acc04c74a01a2c64206711b85562f2df2d7c78cdf504260549a8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 593,
        "sourceEnd": 755,
        "text": "Right. And the study used first-year university students in one city. So we cannot say the result is true for children, or for older adults, or for every country.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "1640ecd18ddda3efd4ec8ccbc251970b3b45921b17bcd53b22e565135e77c96a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 763,
        "sourceEnd": 987,
        "text": "Exactly. A broad conclusion often hides a narrow sample. Now, let me give you the seminar task. In pairs, write one sentence that states the claim, and one sentence that states a limit. Then swap with another pair and check.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "45c5b364806cc5b98c8c5089bc2159f2cf10e44eae046b3177723ffd7b98ce1a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 997,
        "sourceEnd": 1128,
        "text": "I have a small correction. In the reading I sent, the number was forty students, not four hundred. I mistyped it. Please use forty.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "eb0baea425bb9fca0f8918419dd89704d51b5a5e7293d43ce9cfeae43332e6bc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1136,
        "sourceEnd": 1385,
        "text": "Thank you for catching that. Forty students is a small sample. So the second limit is sample size. Now, what about the test itself? The students answered short questions, not essays. So the claim is about short-answer recall, not deep understanding.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "82fa5c45e5dcdb6295ae9b4b80f5748ab11caf6d5d7731bc1046abd68ac391b0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1395,
        "sourceEnd": 1478,
        "text": "So if someone says, \"Handwriting is always better for learning,\" that is too broad.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "5ddc4c8fad88a1b3db5887fcc94fd2e176e8a5a1506cfdfcd1a54024addbe6ae",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1486,
        "sourceEnd": 1752,
        "text": "Yes. That is the kind of sentence we want to test. Here is a better version: \"In one small study, first-year university students who took notes by hand recalled more short-answer facts after one week than students who typed.\" That sentence is long, but it is honest.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "c6e1ce0daa31a0721d3564c663639b015d153a5b2fb642f06ff5d81958e17fed",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1762,
        "sourceEnd": 1914,
        "text": "Can we also talk about the opposite mistake? Some people say, \"Typing is useless.\" That is also too broad. The study did not test typing for every task.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "025748cc97977528b8251021e2bc69c99848a05f33d8ff64201ce7c6a9289f0d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1922,
        "sourceEnd": 2164,
        "text": "Correct. Now, a practical point. When you correct your own grammar mistakes this week, do not just redo the old exercise. After each correction, try a new sentence with the same pattern. That way you test transfer, not memory of the old item.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "183efd61a8eef880cb3debb6128e53dc39ce880ccafe4db946ee18f09b476ae3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2174,
        "sourceEnd": 2334,
        "text": "I like that. So if I wrote \"The study show a small sample,\" and I correct it to \"shows,\" I should then write a new sentence, like \"The report shows two limits.\"",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "e49dd6b27914009e45110d1ce5813362adee794d161108a08018308fcd6e250e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2342,
        "sourceEnd": 2466,
        "text": "Exactly. New sentence, same rule. Now, let me check the time. We have ten minutes left. Please write your two sentences now.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "8249049e323c035dc9887a536523d6ac84a6e378ef69b8f75a98b735b630975a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2476,
        "sourceEnd": 2659,
        "text": "While you write, remember the three limits we found: one-week recall, forty first-year students in one city, and short-answer questions. Do not add limits that the study did not test.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "b951cec578e3353e1256c6da9f8aaa1aaeff2aea370621d991afcbcfe780905f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2667,
        "sourceEnd": 2730,
        "text": "And do not remove limits that it did test. Okay, start writing.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b128e5c490a65f6f5ae770fc569a1407b7c71389a066e5190c274f2e635d02f8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2740,
        "sourceEnd": 2911,
        "text": "One more thing. The study did not compare handwriting with no notes at all. It compared handwriting with typing. So we cannot say handwriting is better than doing nothing.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f46260deada32a9945326a468a0bde05d9e85b8de0abb4a0363b161a945ceb83",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2919,
        "sourceEnd": 2989,
        "text": "Good. That is a fourth limit. Now, pairs, please share your sentences.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "a4b8928d447c94902a832ffa8d81e59603f98bf8667ece375d051e87718f1404",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3000,
        "sourceEnd": 3029,
        "text": "Pair one, what did you write?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "1fd69ad6f938d113dac9068baed0a9321403c5e4311b2b47432d56372b9b2ea7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3037,
        "sourceEnd": 3099,
        "text": "Let us hear from pair one. Then we will compare with pair two.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "120d4a6d4d12b9963ac29b9ca47ff537678217c6cee95038821d8839cb1a29e1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3109,
        "sourceEnd": 3318,
        "text": "Pair one says: \"The study found that handwriting helped short-answer recall after one week.\" That is accurate. Pair two says: \"Handwriting is always better for all learning.\" That is too broad. Can you fix it?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "753aa2b47a30679f2d78763d5bb94e1fe9fa5b6273abda21a8094074e531afbb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3326,
        "sourceEnd": 3359,
        "text": "Pair two, try again with a limit.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e5af20596b9767a6f6bbb89f8e73761072f04c959e31c5a032395cdae8927f57",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 3370,
        "sourceEnd": 3497,
        "text": "They now say: \"In one small study, handwriting helped short-answer recall after one week for first-year students.\" Much better.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "67b4e169b1fb8cb4044df11fffc0ac4ae4ba6e322a29902903694b06652976bf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3505,
        "sourceEnd": 3653,
        "text": "Good work. For next week, bring one broad claim from your own reading and write two limits for it. Remember: correct, then test with a new sentence.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "0103a88c2526af71e95e7436b80c3814b69861853de11193750f3dd743d9be89",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
